   "title": "Models · what goes where",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Models · what goes where\n\nWhen the template opens, ComfyUI offers the files it misses (*Missing models*: download them there). By hand: put each file into its folder below - or into a folder of your `extra_model_paths.yaml`. **0 · System Check** lists what is there and what is missing.\n\n## Needed\n- [pytorch_model.bin](https://huggingface.co/woongzip1/universr-audio/resolve/main/pytorch_model.bin) · 229 MB · CC BY 4.0 (weights); MIT (inference code)  \n  UniverSR audio super-resolution (8/12/16/24 kHz -> 48 kHz, vocoder-free flow matching): HQ 2 · Regenerate Highs in every template's Master when HQ mastering is on (on by default in Enhance & Master), and Refine\n\n## Optional\n- [model_bs_roformer_ep_17_sdr_9.6568.ckpt](https://github.com/ZFTurbo/Music-Source-Separation-Training/releases/download/v1.0.12/model_bs_roformer_ep_17_sdr_9.6568.ckpt) · 527 MB · MIT (trainer); trained on MUSDB18-HQ, whose dataset terms are research-oriented  \n  the *Stems (optional)* block (bypassed: select it and press Ctrl+B)\n\n## Where they go\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n└── 📂 models/\n    ├── 📂 audio_separation/ (stems, the vocal stem for the lyrics times)\n    │   └── model_bs_roformer_ep_17_sdr_9.6568.ckpt\n    └── 📂 audio_sr/\n        └── pytorch_model.bin\n```\n\n## Your computer\n\nEnhance & Master runs on the CPU. HQ mastering (UniverSR) is faster on a graphics card: about 1.5 s per second of music on an RTX 5060 Ti; switched off it needs no model at all.\n\nLicences: [docs/user/licensing.md](https://github.com/jplenio/Plenio-Music-Production-System/blob/main/docs/user/licensing.md) · every file: [docs/user/models.md](https://github.com/jplenio/Plenio-Music-Production-System/blob/main/docs/user/models.md)\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
